[[Colonel]] '''Ward'''<ref name="Celeb swcom">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-celebration-2025-the-mandalorian-and-grogu|text=''The Mandalorian and Grogu'' Kickstart ''Star Wars'' Celebration Japan 2025}}</ref> was a [[human]] individual who served within the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and later in the [[New Republic]] [[New Republic Defense Fleet Starfighter Corps|as a starfighter pilot]] during the [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="Celeb panel" /> During that time, they contacted the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] on [[Adelphi Base]]<ref name="Official Trailer" /> and sent him on a [[mission on the Outer Rim]]<ref name="Gamesradar">{{WebCite|url=https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/star-wars-movies/sigourney-weaver-was-delighted-to-join-the-star-wars-franchise-but-says-grogu-was-the-whole-reason-she-signed-on-for-the-mandalorian-and-grogu-hes-a-little-badass|date=2025-02-07|author=Megan Garside|text=Sigourney Weaver was "delighted" to join the Star Wars franchise but says Grogu was the whole reason she signed on for The Mandalorian & Grogu: "He's a little badass"|archivedate=20250306113614}}</ref> to take out both [[Imperial Remnants|Imperial Remnant]] forces and gangsters of the [[Hutt Clan]].<ref name="Official Trailer" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I play a wonderful character who is, you know, in a position of authority. And I have to send the Mandalorian out on a mission on the Outer Rim where all the bad stuff happens.|Sigourney Weaver on Ward.|<ref name="Gamesradar" />}}
Ward was created for the upcoming [[2026]] movie ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu]]'' and will be portrayed by [[Sigourney Weaver]].<ref name="Getty" /> When Weaver was first approached about the film by director [[Jon Favreau]] in a video meeting, she was shy and admitted that she hadn't watched the prior ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian|The Mandalorian]]'' TV series and Favreau responded that she should start watching the series. Weaver then watched the series and accepted the role in their next meeting. Weaver had previously already stared as the character [[Wikipedia:Ellen Ripley|Ellen Ripley]] in the ''[[Wikipedia:Alien (franchise)|Alien]]'' science fiction horror franchise as well as other blockbuster films and has said that she was glad to still have been considered for a role in a ''[[Star Wars]]'' film, which usually feature lesser-known actors.<ref name="Celeb panel" /> Weaver said that she had never really considered acting ''Star Wars'', but joined because she loved the character of Djarin's apprentice Grogu and has said that really enjoyed working with him<ref name="Gamesradar" /> and got emotional when she first met his puppet on set<ref name="Celeb panel" /> around August [[2024]].<ref name="Deadline">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2024/08/sigourney-weaver-interview-venice-film-festival-golden-lion-award-alien-avatar-1236052005|text=Sigourney Weaver, On Eve Of Her Venice Lifetime Achievement Award, Lifts Lid On Remarkable Career From 'Alien' To 'Avatar', 'Working Girl' To 'Ghostbusters' And 'Star Wars' Role To Come|author=Andreas Wiseman|date=2024-08-27|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20240828022426}}</ref>

Weaver first revealed her role as part of the film during an interview on [[August 27]], 2024 and began filming sometime afterwards with the production wrapped by early December.<ref name="FilmingWrap">{{WebCite|author=Molly Brizell|date=2024-12-03|url=https://screenrant.com/star-wars-the-mandalorian-and-grogu-finished-filming|text=Star Wars' Next Movie Has Finished Filming, Lucasfilm Boss Teases Grogu's Future|archivedate=20241203212404|work=[[Wikipedia:Screen Rant|''Screen Rant'']]}}</ref> Still footage of Ward was later shown exclusively to audiences at during [[Celebration Japan (2025)|Celebration Japan]] on [[April 18]], [[2025]].<ref name="Celeb swcom" /> The character was later first publicly featured in the teaser trailer released on [[September 22]] of that year<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|_pa1KLXuW0Y|The Mandalorian and Grogu &#124; Official Trailer &#124; In Theaters May 22, 2026}}</ref> and identified in an accompanying image released by [[The Walt Disney Company|The Walt Disney Studios]] on [[Wikipedia:Getty Images|Getty Images]] and in an article on [[StarWars.com]], both released that same day.<ref name="Teaser swcom">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-mandalorian-and-grogu-trailer-key-art-1|text=''The Mandalorian and Grogu'' First Teaser Trailer Revealed}}</ref>

